No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent John Carter (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Texas's 31st District, anchored in the Austin area's northern suburbs and the Killeen-Temple region, leans Republican by about eleven points. Incumbent John Carter is seeking another term after turning back a crowded GOP primary that drew nine challengers, including Vince Offer, the 'ShamWow' pitchman. Every one of the ten expert ratings tracked calls the seat Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Democrat Justin Early roughly a five percent chance of winning.\n\nEarly, a first-time candidate, has raised about $292,000 to Carter's $1.5 million, and neither side has attracted meaningful outside spending. Green candidate Greg Stoker is also on the ballot but has limited resources. With no public general-election polls, the outlook rests on the district's lean, the money gap, and the unanimous expert consensus. A Democratic-leaning national environment keeps this from being an afterthought, but the evidence points firmly toward Carter's reelection.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0328, "margin": -14.67}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0442, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0454, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.036, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0275, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0304, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0331, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0323, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0129, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0246, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0251, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0249, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0403, "margin": -12.6}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0208, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0404, "margin": -12.0